{"name":"Gravelstone","hex":"#d3c7b8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Conglomerate (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"Conglomerate is a sedimentary rock made up of rounded gravel-sized pieces of rock surrounded by finer-grained sediments. The larger fragments within conglomerate are called clasts, while the finer sediment surrounding the clasts is called the matrix. The clasts and matrix are typically cemented by calcium carbonate, iron oxide, silica, or hardened clay."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ferruginous_quartz-pebble_conglomerate_%28derived_from_boulder_in_%22Sharon_Conglomerate%22%2C_Lower_Pennsylvanian%3B_Jackson_North_roadcut%2C_Ohio%2C_USA%29_30.jpg/330px-Ferruginous_quartz-pebble_conglomerate_%28derived_from_boulder_in_%22Sharon_Conglomerate%22%2C_Lower_Pennsylvanian%3B_Jackson_North_roadcut%2C_Ohio%2C_USA%29_30.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conglomerate_(geology)","wikidata":"Q191704"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Carmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg/500px-Carmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Carmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg/1280px-Carmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Carmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg/500px-Carmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carmelo Formation (conglomerate) at Point Lobos","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarmelo_Formation_at_Point_Lobos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Sangjunak1.jpg/500px-Sangjunak1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm